WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:06.510
Hey, David, if Trump doesn't run in 2024 24,
could Tucker Carlson be the future of Trump

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:08.950
ism and or the Republican Party?

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:15.340
So at this point, before I even talk about
Tucker, anybody who hears that question and

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:22.619
says Tucker Carlson, Fox News propagandist
could never be the Republican nominee seems

00:00:22.619 --> 00:00:23.619
premature.

00:00:23.619 --> 00:00:29.349
I am nowhere near as confident as people saying
that about those proclamations.

00:00:29.349 --> 00:00:31.239
Look at 2016.

00:00:31.239 --> 00:00:38.200
OK, who would have thought a few years prior
that Trump would be the Republican nominee?

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:41.690
You know, forget about president, but the
Republican nominee.

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:46.740
So if you say, listen, it could be Tucker,
listen, it could be Don Jr..

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:50.590
Listen, it could be the my pillow guy.

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:55.150
I would rule nothing out at this point because
if the Republican electorate has proven anything

00:00:55.150 --> 00:01:01.880
over the last four years, it's that they can
be bamboozled into choosing almost quite literally

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:07.240
anyone, maybe not anyone, but almost anyone
as their nominee.

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:12.189
And they've proven that by how easily they
were bamboozled by Donald Trump in 2016.

00:01:12.189 --> 00:01:18.110
Now, Tucker, specifically in twenty twenty
four first, I think it's too early.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:22.659
And the reason it's too early is that 2024
is going to likely be more about coalitions

00:01:22.659 --> 00:01:23.850
than the individual.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:28.049
So could it be that the coalitions get behind,
Tucker?

00:01:28.049 --> 00:01:29.049
Sure.

00:01:29.049 --> 00:01:31.759
Could it be that the coalitions get behind
Marco Rubio?

00:01:31.759 --> 00:01:32.759
Maybe.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:36.119
Could it be that they get behind, you know,
the my pillow guy?

00:01:36.119 --> 00:01:42.189
The reason I would rule nothing out is that
you have actual Trump cultists right now.

00:01:42.189 --> 00:01:48.579
These are the people chanting Fox News sucks
outside of voting vote count locations.

00:01:48.579 --> 00:01:52.109
These are the people who email me and they
say, David, don't you realize Trump is getting

00:01:52.109 --> 00:01:54.079
four more years?

00:01:54.079 --> 00:01:57.810
You've got the Trump cultists, you then have
the Republican loyalists.

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:02.670
Now, I'm kind of slicing and dicing this a
little bit differently than I often do.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:07.360
Often I say you've got the pro-business people,
the libertarian people and the evangelical

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.479
religious right.

00:02:08.479 --> 00:02:11.090
This is different because it's more voting
contingencies.

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:17.640
I'm talking about Trump cultists, Republican
loyalists in which I include the social conservatives,

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:24.380
the evangelical types, et cetera, people who
are more on cultural issues and because of

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:27.120
socialism and so on, voting for Republicans.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:31.870
And then I've got these kind of economic conservatives
and those are the people that were most likely

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:39.020
to not like Trump because they found all of
the other stuff pretty distasteful.

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:44.390
It's people who basically want relatively
low regulation and lower taxes and business

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:48.930
freedom, but they're not social conservatives
and they find Trump to be a buffoon.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:56.430
I think that that first group, the Trump cultists,
mostly disappears unless Trump simply keeps

00:02:56.430 --> 00:03:02.220
going and campaigns all through the next four
years and runs in twenty, twenty four to once

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:04.170
again be the Republican nominee.

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:10.930
If Trump doesn't do that, I believe that the
Trump cultists are the group that will determine

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:15.100
whether the Republican Party goes back to,
like, you know, Jeb, that type of thing in

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:21.210
twenty, twenty four, or whether Trump or someone
wacky could be the nominee again.

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:26.730
Do the Trump cultists become normal conservative
Republicans?

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:32.950
Do the Trump cultists fragment and take away
from the Republican Party by creating some

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:34.330
new coalition?

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:38.530
Do the Trump called this, many of which were
never even paying attention to politics before

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:39.530
Trump?

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:43.080
Do they just get back out of politics altogether
and go back to wherever they were before?

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:50.470
I do think it would be a mistake to say that
it was only Trump's celebrity prior to 2016

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:51.470
that gave him the cult.

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:56.870
Like following the celebrity may well have
helped, but what really gave Trump the cult

00:03:56.870 --> 00:04:02.120
like following was that he tapped into these
ideas that were really bolstered during the

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:08.680
Obama era, including just standard racism,
but also the idea of working class whites

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:13.930
feeling like they are losing privileged status,
not saying that they rightly felt that, but

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:15.569
they felt it.

00:04:15.569 --> 00:04:22.030
And the sort of xenophobic stuff that was
often kind of scattered and not above the

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:27.410
surface, Trump was able to say to all those
people, come to the surface, say this stuff

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:29.600
publicly, you are with me.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:31.270
That's how he developed the cult.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:34.150
Like following the celebrity certainly helped.

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:38.130
And so I think those are all factors we have
to think about going into twenty, twenty four.

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.760
But I would rule out nothing.

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.980
In terms of could it be, Tucker?

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:43.980
Sure.

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:46.410
Could it be, you know, Ivanka, it could be.

00:04:46.410 --> 00:06:09.370
I would rule nothing out at this point.

